WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:02.616
(soft music)

00:00:05.183 --> 00:00:08.006
- I'm Kelly Bathe, I have
two mixed-race children,

00:00:08.006 --> 00:00:09.976
half-Irish and half Black.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:13.987
- My name is Kathy Weiss, and
I have a 34-year old daughter

00:00:13.987 --> 00:00:17.603
and a 27-year old son,
Jeremy, who is adopted.

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:20.658
- My name is Shelly Patrick,
and I'm the mother of two sons.

00:00:20.658 --> 00:00:22.232
They're my biological children.

00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:24.989
- My name is Frank Cayetti,
and I have two children.

00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:26.756
A 6 and a half year old
daughter named Lucy,

00:00:26.756 --> 00:00:30.120
and a 3 and a half year old
adopted son named Joseph.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.176
- My husband and I started
dating when we were in

00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:34.515
our thirties, and we never
really thought about the fact

00:00:34.515 --> 00:00:37.211
that we were a mixed-race
couple until we decided

00:00:37.211 --> 00:00:38.414
to have children.

00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:40.828
My kids were gonna face
situations that I just didn't know

00:00:40.828 --> 00:00:43.565
how to navigate because I
had never faced them myself.

00:00:43.565 --> 00:00:46.025
I remember just sobbing,
and my husband taking me

00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:48.919
in his arms, and telling me
that it's not my job to teach

00:00:48.919 --> 00:00:53.297
my son to be a black
man, that it's his job.

00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:56.691
That it's my job to teach my
kids respect, and kindness

00:00:56.691 --> 00:00:58.707
just like every other mother
in the world, regardless

00:00:58.707 --> 00:00:59.806
of what color my skin is.

00:00:59.806 --> 00:01:02.315
- We tried to have another child.

00:01:02.315 --> 00:01:06.815
There were issues with me
that was not gonna enable us

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.170
to have another biological child.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.409
Social workers actually came
out with a policy against

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:15.542
transracial adoptions.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:20.126
There was a strong belief
that white families couldn't

00:01:20.126 --> 00:01:24.439
provide what black children
needed for their own identity.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:26.894
We did not live the black
experience in America and

00:01:26.894 --> 00:01:31.477
how do we provide him some
connection to what the world

00:01:32.631 --> 00:01:37.078
sees him as, even if his
personal experience is slightly

00:01:37.078 --> 00:01:38.451
different than that?

00:01:38.451 --> 00:01:40.420
- We wanted to adopt for many reasons.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.204
My wife was very much compelled,
she has an adopted brother

00:01:43.204 --> 00:01:46.633
and she worked at a nonprofit
that worked with a lot of

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:48.068
former foster youths.

00:01:48.068 --> 00:01:50.249
We talked about trying to
have a biological child first,

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:53.006
and then the next thing we
were interested in doing is

00:01:53.006 --> 00:01:53.905
adopting.

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:56.695
I was talking to a woman I
met at a theater opening.

00:01:56.695 --> 00:01:59.746
She's African-American, the
subject of my kids came up

00:01:59.746 --> 00:02:01.259
because I love talking about them.

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:03.378
She asked, point-blank, which
is a really good question:

00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:07.018
are you going to allow some
influence in his life from

00:02:07.018 --> 00:02:08.594
other African-American people?

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:12.124
I was kind of stumped for
a second and then realized

00:02:12.124 --> 00:02:13.535
I absolutely have to.

00:02:13.535 --> 00:02:16.430
- I was only about 20 when I had Jason.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.682
I don't know if it was my
immaturity, but I didn't really

00:02:18.682 --> 00:02:21.983
look at my kids as
black, or white, or half,

00:02:21.983 --> 00:02:24.691
I just looked at them as my children.

00:02:24.691 --> 00:02:27.191
When I was going through my
divorce, I'm seeing a therapist

00:02:27.191 --> 00:02:30.148
at the time, she pointed
out how important it was

00:02:30.148 --> 00:02:33.767
for the children to have
regular time with their father

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:36.739
and his side of the
family, so that they could

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:39.742
learn the nonverbal
communication skills of

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.185
the black culture.

00:02:41.185 --> 00:02:44.112
So that was something I
was always mindful of and

00:02:44.112 --> 00:02:45.485
made sure that that happened.

00:02:45.485 --> 00:02:48.463
- Consultation is just an admission that

00:02:48.463 --> 00:02:49.633
you don't know everything.

00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:52.837
It doesn't make me feel weird
at all-- it makes me a little

00:02:52.837 --> 00:02:56.230
sad to think that he's going
to have some experiences

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.803
that I can't entirely relate to.

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:03.054
- My daughters hair was
definitely a learning experience.

00:03:03.054 --> 00:03:05.883
I have a niece who also
has a mixed-race daughter.

00:03:05.883 --> 00:03:08.919
She actually has given
me so much information.

00:03:08.919 --> 00:03:12.709
YouTube tutorials, Pinterest,
learning what co washing is,

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:16.096
just making her realize
how precious and amazing

00:03:16.096 --> 00:03:17.517
her hair is.

00:03:17.517 --> 00:03:20.841
- I don't think we would
have thought about moving

00:03:20.841 --> 00:03:23.227
out of Philadelphia for a minute.

00:03:23.227 --> 00:03:25.578
Jeremy wouldn't feel
out of place growing up,

00:03:25.578 --> 00:03:27.705
he would see other people
that looked liked him,

00:03:27.705 --> 00:03:31.897
family friends and personal
friends, and teachers.

00:03:31.897 --> 00:03:35.548
You know, we were always
aware of that strong presence

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.498
in his life.

00:03:36.498 --> 00:03:38.751
He would have the resources,
he would go somewhere

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.852
if he needed to figure things out.

00:03:40.852 --> 00:03:42.826
- MY husband has had to teach me.

00:03:42.826 --> 00:03:45.642
I have taken on his thoughts
on this, that you would

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:48.013
rather know who's a racist
because now you know

00:03:48.013 --> 00:03:48.969
who to stay away from.

00:03:48.969 --> 00:03:51.966
It's the ones who aren't
saying it, but are thinking it

00:03:51.966 --> 00:03:53.623
are the ones that are the real issues.

00:03:53.623 --> 00:03:58.012
- When Jeremy was a very
young child, strangers would

00:03:58.012 --> 00:04:00.161
come up to us and say,
"Oh, he's gonna be a

00:04:00.161 --> 00:04:01.880
great ball player isn't he?"

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.598
at some point I would say,
why, because he's black?

00:04:05.598 --> 00:04:08.343
At other points, I just
got fed up with it and said

00:04:08.343 --> 00:04:10.713
no, he's actually gonna
be a brain surgeon.

00:04:10.713 --> 00:04:13.402
It is stunning to me what
comes out of people's mouths

00:04:13.402 --> 00:04:15.568
and I am still not quiet about it.

00:04:15.568 --> 00:04:19.972
- I recall this one time I
went to look at a townhouse.

00:04:19.972 --> 00:04:23.611
When I went into view it
with the realtor, a person

00:04:23.611 --> 00:04:28.236
who lived there came in
and he was like, saying

00:04:28.236 --> 00:04:31.326
"Oh this is a great complex,
and you'll like living

00:04:31.326 --> 00:04:34.831
here, and we don't have
any" and he used the n-word,

00:04:34.831 --> 00:04:36.868
"that live here."

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:38.605
I'm gonna get choked up.

00:04:38.605 --> 00:04:42.197
And I said, well I will
not be renting here because

00:04:42.197 --> 00:04:45.478
I have two half-black
children, and it would make

00:04:45.478 --> 00:04:48.238
me nervous to have them
here with somebody that

00:04:48.238 --> 00:04:49.335
thinks that way.

00:04:49.335 --> 00:04:51.377
Some white people just let
it roll off, but when you

00:04:51.377 --> 00:04:53.423
have children, you
don't just let it slide.

00:04:53.423 --> 00:04:56.082
- You teach your kids tact,
and you teach your kids

00:04:56.082 --> 00:04:58.757
that ignorance is
everywhere, and unfortunately

00:04:58.757 --> 00:05:02.004
I'm not gonna be able to
save them from everything.

00:05:02.004 --> 00:05:05.472
- It has been very important
for me to talk to Jeremy.

00:05:05.472 --> 00:05:08.049
He had one incident where
somebody said something

00:05:08.049 --> 00:05:10.389
to him, I think when
he was around 11 or 12,

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:14.051
and he never told us, and
dealt with it probably

00:05:14.051 --> 00:05:15.924
by talking to his friends.

00:05:15.924 --> 00:05:19.588
I felt like I had failed
him, his friends maybe

00:05:19.588 --> 00:05:21.056
were a better resource.

00:05:21.056 --> 00:05:24.507
I felt like, sheesh, why can't
he talk to me about this?

00:05:24.507 --> 00:05:27.906
- You have to teach, and you
have to talk to your kids

00:05:27.906 --> 00:05:29.097
about police brutality.

00:05:29.097 --> 00:05:33.031
You have to talk to your
kids about racist undertones.

00:05:33.031 --> 00:05:35.715
I would rather have
the conversation before

00:05:35.715 --> 00:05:38.583
anybody else has it with her, so that she

00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:40.557
understands where we stand.

00:05:40.557 --> 00:05:43.139
- The interesting thing
that I think I've observed

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:45.343
about race, is I have a privilege to not

00:05:45.343 --> 00:05:47.783
be cognizant of it and others do not.

00:05:47.783 --> 00:05:51.782
I have to be empathetic
to my son in that regard.

00:05:51.782 --> 00:05:54.785
The issues that Joseph
may face terrifies me;

00:05:54.785 --> 00:05:58.219
someday I'm gonna have to have
a real tough conversation,

00:05:58.219 --> 00:06:01.075
now I just want him to be
the happiest 3 and a half

00:06:01.075 --> 00:06:02.305
year old kid out there.

00:06:02.305 --> 00:06:05.083
- My husband, being a
black parent, he had talks

00:06:05.083 --> 00:06:08.517
with them, but a few
times, when they came home

00:06:08.517 --> 00:06:11.326
and told me they had been
called a racial name,

00:06:11.326 --> 00:06:13.962
it really upset me, but
then when they told me

00:06:13.962 --> 00:06:16.629
how they handled it, I
was so proud of them.

00:06:16.629 --> 00:06:20.235
I knew that they were equipped
and strong to handle it.

00:06:20.235 --> 00:06:22.471
- Jeremy definitely had identity issues,

00:06:22.471 --> 00:06:24.269
I don't think it was all smooth sailing

00:06:24.269 --> 00:06:27.952
and everything's been "Leave
it to Beaver" nice for him.

00:06:27.952 --> 00:06:31.144
He had to figure out what it meant

00:06:31.144 --> 00:06:35.144
to be a black man in
America with a white family

00:06:36.363 --> 00:06:40.196
and a Jewish background,
because he walks into

00:06:41.216 --> 00:06:44.393
a room and the narrative is written.

00:06:44.393 --> 00:06:48.017
He's always struggling
with his own definition

00:06:48.017 --> 00:06:50.991
against a public definition is of him.

00:06:50.991 --> 00:06:53.374
- So my hope for the future
is, you know, we start

00:06:53.374 --> 00:06:54.959
to evolve as a nation.

00:06:54.959 --> 00:06:57.249
- When you see children playing together,

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:59.737
they may be cognizant of the difference

00:06:59.737 --> 00:07:02.818
in the way that they
look, but I don't think

00:07:02.818 --> 00:07:04.977
there's any preconceived
notion, I think that

00:07:04.977 --> 00:07:07.070
racism is a learned behavior.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.682
- My hope for my children
is that they grow up

00:07:09.682 --> 00:07:13.041
and they learn to be kind, and
they learn to be respectful.

00:07:13.041 --> 00:07:18.041
- Jeremy's trying to make it
in the world of music right now

00:07:18.197 --> 00:07:22.269
I think he has great talent,
but I'm a party of one

00:07:22.269 --> 00:07:23.720
with a little bit of bias.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.724
- I just want them to feel
safe and feel loved, and

00:07:26.724 --> 00:07:28.185
secure in who they are.

00:07:28.185 --> 00:07:31.626
- I hope that my children
are successful, and enjoy

00:07:31.626 --> 00:07:34.126
their lives as they have fun.

